\title{Asking Disco for types}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{We can ask Disco what type something has with the \tt{:type} command. For example, if we ask for the type of a number like \tt{3}, Disco tells us it has type #{\N} (which stands for the [[002D]]):
\pre\verb<<<|
Disco> :type 3
3 : ℕ<<<
}
